{
  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted → acc 0.542), the evidence is extremely sparse and the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal combination is actually contributing over a strong unimodal baseline. config_036 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is the cleanest ablation of config_001: it keeps the same RNA encoder (scgpt), same profile setting (multiprofile), and same aggregation (avgpool), removing only the image branch and fusion. If RNA-only achieves accuracy close to 0.542, the image modality is not adding value and I should pivot to cheaper RNA-focused or image-focused configs for the remaining 8 experiments. If it drops substantially, multimodal is confirmed as the right direction and I can then explore fusion/aggregation/encoder variants within the multimodal family. Expected cost: roughly 1.5–2.0 GPU hours (no ViT-L image forward/backward), making it cheaper than config_001 while answering the highest-leverage design question early in the budget."
}

